WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.621
Large vision models trained by autoregression
promise a single generalist model for many visual tasks,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:13.322
but today's versions demand billions of parameters
and hundreds of billions of visual tokens to train.

00:00:13.402 --> 00:00:17.659
This ICML 2024 paper, DeLVM, asks whether we really
need all that.

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:20.943
The authors show that two simple, classical ideas,

00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:23.900
data augmentation and knowledge distillation,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.681
let a compact autoregressive vision model reach
strong performance on a limited dataset,

00:00:29.761 --> 00:00:35.200
cutting both the parameter footprint and the
training data requirement dramatically.
